AI decisions affect people's lives, so ethics keeps AI beneficial and not harmful:
- prevents bias and discrimination (fairness);
- protects privacy and user data;
- makes systems accountable, transparent and safe, which builds trust.

Without laws, technologies can be misused or give unfair outcomes. Laws and policies:
- define how data is collected, stored and used;
- protect privacy and individuals' rights (e.g. GDPR);
- ensure fair, accountable use and build public trust.
